# C++ style

Apply these rules to first-party sources. This repository is C: a WDM kernel driver and a user-mode tool. Use the rules that compile as C. Do not introduce C++-only syntax (`std::`, brace initialization, `constexpr`, `noexcept`, `nullptr`, `using`, or `[[nodiscard]]`) into these sources.

- Brace-initialize objects: `Vector{ x, y }`, `std::size_t count{ 0U }`. Keep parentheses when braces change meaning, such as `std::vector<T>(count)` or a constructor that would be narrowed by braces.
- Suffix unsigned indices, sizes, and unsigned constants by value: `U` through 4294967295, `ULL` above that. Do not suffix signed, floating, or character literals.
- Mark default constructors and constructors callable with zero or one argument `explicit`. Leave copy and move constructors implicit. Do not add a constructor to an aggregate.
- Mark a function `constexpr` when its body is a constant expression.
- Mark parameters and locals `const` when they are not modified.
- Mark a function `[[nodiscard]]` when ignoring its result is a mistake. Skip `void` functions.
- Mark a function `noexcept` only when it cannot throw, including through functions it calls. Do not mark functions that allocate, lock, stream, or throw.
- Put `if`, `for`, `while`, `do`, and `else` bodies in `{}` blocks.
- Prefer the C++ library over the C library: `std::memcpy`, `std::memset`, `std::sin`, `std::abs`. Call an OS or C function with `::` only when C++ has no equivalent, as in `::gmtime_s`.
- Prefer `std::array` to a C-style array. Pass `.data()` when a C interface needs a pointer.
- Name fixed-width integers and `size_t` in `std`: `std::uint32_t`, `std::int64_t`, `std::size_t`.
- Mark an unused parameter or local `[[maybe_unused]]` and keep its name. Do not silence it with a `(void)` cast or by omitting the name.
- Cast with `static_cast`, `const_cast`, `reinterpret_cast`, or `dynamic_cast`. Do not use a C-style cast.
- Prefer preincrement and predecrement: `++index`, `--index`. Keep the postfix form when the previous value is the result, as in `path[depth++] = slot`, `return id++`, or `operator++(int)`.
- Prefer `using` to `typedef`. Leave a `typedef` that is part of a C API.
- Prefer `nullptr` to `NULL`.
- Parenthesize each operand of `&&` and `||` when that operand is a comparison or another compound expression: `(index > 0U) && (index < count)`.
- Group includes, with one blank line between groups, and sort each group lexicographically. An implementation file starts with its associated header. Then other project headers, then external non-OS headers, then OS headers, then C and C++ standard headers. Project headers use quotes. Every other header uses angle brackets. Keep every OS header in one guard chain: `#ifdef` for the first operating system and `#elif defined(...)` for each other operating system that has headers. Inside the Windows branch, include `<winsock2.h>` before `<Windows.h>`.

```cpp
#include "Widget.h"

#include "Other.h"
#include "Utility.h"

#include <asio.hpp>
#include <gtest/gtest.h>

#ifdef _WIN32
#include <winsock2.h>
#include <Windows.h>
#elif defined(__linux__)
#include <sys/socket.h>
#elif defined(__APPLE__)
#include <sys/socket.h>
#endif

#include <algorithm>
#include <cstdint>
#include <vector>
```

